## Tolerances and boundaries
RelTol 0.1 Relative tolerance of the adaptive differentiation scheme 0.1
Flux_tol 0.2 Tolerance of mass balance assumption per cell mg N m-3 0.1
min_pool 0.0025 Minimum pool size 0.00000001
min_dens 1e-17 Minimum density of top predators and fish 0.0001
min_channel_depth 0.001 Minimum depth of estuarine channels
## Biological parameters
# Primary producer growth
mum_GRN_T15 1.0 #0.75 Maximum growth rate, small (pico) phytoplankton d-1 1 - 1.24
mum_DIA_T15 1.0 #0.8 Maximum growth rate, diatoms d-1 0.3 - 0.8
# Primary producer light requirements
KI_GRN_T15 10 Light saturation, small phytoplankton W m-2 180 10 - 20
KI_DIA_T15 10 Light saturation, diatoms W m-2 120 10 - 20
eddy_scale 1 Coefficient scaling eddy strength impact on phytoplankton growth 1
# Primary producer nutrient requirements
KN_GRN 1.5 Half-sat const for GRN growth on DIN mg N m-3 117.18 4
KN_DIA 1.8 Half-sat const for DIA growth on DIN mg N m-3 30
KS_GRN 1e-7 Half-sat const for GRN growth on Si mg Si m-3 0
KS_DIA 1e-7 Half-sat const for DIA growth on Si mg Si m-3 0
KF_GRN 0 Half-sat const for GRN growth on Micro-nutrient mg Fe m-3 0
KF_DIA 0 Half-sat const for DIA growth on Micro-nutrient mg Fe m-3 0
KP_GRN 4 #18.231 Half-sat const for GRN growth on Phosphorus mg P m-3 4
KP_DIA 10 #71.07 Half-sat const for DIA growth on Phosphorus mg P m-3 30
#KC was added on Aug 24 2023 using setas example
KC_GRM 1.31 From ERGOM,Half-sat const for PS growth on P mg P m-3 0
KC_DIA 3.49 From ERGOM,Half-sat const for PC growth on P mg P m-3 0
# Bacterial nutrient requirements
KN_BB 5 Half-sat const for sediment bacteria NH uptake mg N m-3 0 - 10
# Bacterial population parameters (how much bacterial biomass detritus can support)
XPB_DL 0.27 Maximum ratio of PB to DL biomass 0.3 - 0.4
XBB_DL 0.18 Maximum ratio of BB to DL biomass 0.15 - 0.2
XPB_DR 0.012 Maximum ratio of PB to DR biomass 0.01 - 0.015
XBB_DR 0.008 Maximum ratio of BB to DR biomass 0.005 - 0.01
k_PB 3 Shape of PB growth eq'n, 1 = linear, 3 = drop before max, 5 = drop at max 3
k_BB 3 Shape of BB growth eq'n, 1 = linear, 3 = drop before max, 5 = drop at max 3
BBthresh 10 Threshold BB flux level where damping starts mg N m-2 s-1 0.1
BBdamp 0.85 Damping coefficient for BB fluxes 0.75
# Space restrictions for basal (epibenthic and some infauna) groups
CHImax 20000 Maximum deposit feeder biomass mg N m-2 500000
DREmax 20000 Maximum deep filter feeder biomass mg N m-2 1000
## pH effects
flagpHchange 0 Whether the pH values change through time following a forced trend - yes = 1, no = 0
# Threshold spatial factors for filter feeders if using ERSEM formulation
DRE_low 200 Little space limitation (pop too small) mg.N.m-2 2000
DRE_sat 30000 Interference to uptake due to shading mg.N.m-2 2500
DREthresh 8000 mg.N.m-2 1000
-------
#SPH_low 500 Little space limitation (pop too small) mg.N.m-2 2500
#SPH_sat 3000 Interference to uptake due to shading mg.N.m-2 3000
#SPHthresh 5000 mg.N.m-2 1000
#DIP_low 200 Little space limitation (pop too small) mg.N.m-2 2000
#DIP_sat 3000 Interference to uptake due to shading mg.N.m-2 2500
#DIPthresh 5000 mg.N.m-2 1000
#CHI_low 2000 Little space limitation (pop too small) mg.N.m-2 2000
#CHI_sat 30000 Interference to uptake due to shading mg.N.m-2 2500
#CHIthresh 50000 mg.N.m-2 1000
